   Results pass directly through the existing store, residual or gate epilogue.
 - At 1024 columns and above, a bounded weight image feeds cuBLASLt. GEMM
   accumulation and output are FP32, followed by the existing epilogue/BF16 cast.
+  Each 32-byte image slice is written as two aligned 128-bit stores. This keeps
+  the scalar decoder's exact FP8 bytes/scales and the existing 64 MiB slab limit;
+  it adds no model copy, codebook allocation or workspace. Independent weight
+  codec tests cover all eight formats, signed/zero/subnormal/maximal finite
+  scales, padded rows and real K, alongside public-Op FP64 and Graph checks.
 
 The backend's existing device profiles can select the Q8 integer matrix route
 instead of the tile. Keys are `gguf_prefill_mxfp8/<format>/<N>x<K>/<epilogue>`;
